Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for React/Vite project

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics by following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package version 1.4.1
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `frontend/src/main.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component within the ToastProvider wrapper in the React component tree
- The Analytics component is now rendered alongside the RouterProvider, ensuring it tracks all page views across the application

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications:
- Used the React-specific package export `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the Analytics component at the root level of the application to ensure it captures all navigation events
- The component is positioned within the provider tree but outside the router, allowing it to track all routes including authentication pages

## Framework Compatibility
This project uses:
- React 19.2.8
- Vite 8.1.5
- React Router 7.18.1

The Analytics component is compatible with React Router and will automatically track page views when users navigate between routes.

## Build Verification
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- TypeScript compilation passed
- All existing functionality preserved
- No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
- No test failures (no tests configured in project)

## Next Steps
To activate analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
4. After deployment, verify the setup by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
5. Monitor visitor data in the Vercel Analytics dashboard

